      "| `XUM_TOOL_INPUT_FILTER`         | `filter`         | string  | Optional regex to filter output lines. By default, only matching lines are returned. When filter_exclude is true, matching lines are excluded instead. Non-matching lines are permanently discarded and cannot be retrieved later.                                                                                                                                                                                 |",
      "| `XUM_TOOL_INPUT_FILTER_EXCLUDE` | `filter_exclude` | boolean | When true, lines matching 'filter' are excluded instead of kept. Key behavior: excluded lines do NOT cause early return from timeout - waiting continues until non-excluded output arrives or process exits. Use to avoid busy polling on progress spam (e.g., filter='⏳\\|waiting\\|\\.\\.\\.' with filter_exclude=true lets you set a long timeout and only wake on meaningful output). Requires 'filter' to be set. |",
      "| `XUM_TOOL_INPUT_PROCESS_ID`     | `process_id`     | string  | The ID of the background process to retrieve output from                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |",
      "| `XUM_TOOL_INPUT_TIMEOUT_SECS`   | `timeout_secs`   | number  | Seconds to wait for new output. If no output is immediately available and process is still running, blocks up to this duration. Returns early when output arrives or process exits. Only use long timeouts (&gt;15s) when no other useful work can be done in parallel.                                                                                                                                            |",
